tive-UkK0V6 avatar-u8q6xB last-JfNEJ_\" style=\"--scale: 36px;\"><div title=\"Christopher Dring\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-width-36 pc-height-36 pc-justifyContent-center pc-alignItems-center pc-position-relative pc-reset bg-secondary-UUD3_J flex-auto-j3S2WA outline-detail-vcQLyr pc-borderRadius-full overflow-hidden-WdpwT6 sizing-border-box-DggLA4 container-TAtrWj\" style=\"--scale: 36px;\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!5onC!,w_36,h_36,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F2bed8dde-a353-40ba-ab27-7d3f3f38d4ff_1440x960.jpeg\" alt=\"Christopher Dring's avatar\" width=\"36\" height=\"36\" draggable=\"false\" class=\"img-OACg1c object-fit-cover-u4ReeV pencraft pc-reset\"></picture></div></div></a></div></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-primary-zABazT line-height-20-t4M0El font-meta-MWBumP size-11-NuY2Zx weight-medium-fw81nC transform-uppercase-yKDgcq reset-IxiVJZ meta-EgzBVA\"><span data-state=\"closed\" style=\"min-width: 0px;\"><a href=\"https://substack.com/@christopherdring\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset decoration-hover-underline-ClDVRM reset-IxiVJZ\">Christopher Dring</a></span></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-4 pc-reset\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-ls1g8s line-height-20-t4M0El font-meta-MWBumP size-11-NuY2Zx weight-medium-fw81nC transform-uppercase-yKDgcq reset-IxiVJZ meta-EgzBVA\"><time datetime=\"2026-09-07T09:22:19.870Z\" title=\"2026-09-07T09:22:19.870Z\">Sep 07, 2026</time></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-secondary-ls1g8s line-height-20-t4M0El font-meta-MWBumP size-11-NuY2Zx weight-medium-fw81nC transform-uppercase-yKDgcq reset-IxiVJZ meta-EgzBVA\">∙ Paid</div></div></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-16 pc-paddingTop-16 pc-paddingBottom-16 pc-justifyContent-space-between pc-alignItems-center pc-reset flex-grow-rzmknG border-top-detail-themed-k9TZAY border-bottom-detail-themed-Ua9186 post-ufi\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><div class=\"like-button-container post-ufi-button style-button\"></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"></div></div></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-16 pc-paddingTop-16 pc-reset\"><div class=\"postContentWrapper-MYe7fH\"><div class=\"dt-post-body\"><div class=\"available-content\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"body markup\"><p><em>Hello there!</em></p><p><em>Over, the last week, I’ve read far too many opinions on the future direction of the video game industry. It’s all Roblox. Or Steam. It’s definitely not console. It’s certainly not live service. It’s mostly China, and a bit of Korea. The jobs are all leaving California and going to India. Kids don’t want pretty graphics. Or long games. And the video game media is finished.</em></p><p><em>Now, whenever I read those things, there’s a little voice in my brain that goes ‘yeah, but…’</em></p><p><em>So, this week, I am going to be talking about trends. Plus, rounding up some big stories, including Xbox Game Pass’s new streaming caps and PlayStation’s latest State of Play.</em></p><p><em>Let’s go!</em></p><div><hr></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Eg0o!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2481527-95bc-479e-96ca-38d2714a436d_2942x1586.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\" class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img can-restack\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Eg0o!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2481527-95bc-479e-96ca-38d2714a436d_2942x1586.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"785\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c2481527-95bc-479e-96ca-38d2714a436d_2942x1586.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:785,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:7826205,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://www.thegamebusiness.com/i/214482389?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fc2481527-95bc-479e-96ca-38d2714a436d_2942x1586.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" alt=\"\" class=\"sizing-normal\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The industry loves a trend.</p><p>Of course it does. Investors like to back businesses that are capitalizing on the new ‘thing’. And tapping into that can be the difference between finding an audience and disappearing without a trace.</p><p>For a good few years, indie publishers would tell me that their job is to ‘put games in the best position to get lucky’. Luck isn’t the best business strategy, but there’s a truth to it. You can say the right things, tick all the marketing boxes, make a brilliant game, and still fail to make any money. And in 2026, that’s almost as true for AAA games as it is for indie projects.</p><p>Therefore, if there’s a trend (whether that’s a game trend, a business trend, or a marketing trend) that can increase your chances of success, then you better chase it. Quick, everyone make a Souls-like or an extraction shooter. What do you mean your game’s not free-to-play? Or $30? Where’s your co-op mode? Why haven’t you set-up a Discord channel yet?</p></div></div><div class=\"visibility-check\"></div></div></div></div></div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset border-left-detail-themed-TuEvbU sidebar-RUDMha\"><div aria-label=\"Sidebar content\" role=\"complementary\" class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-32 pc-reset\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-24 pc-paddingLeft-16 pc-paddingRight-16 pc-paddingTop-24 pc-paddingBottom-24 pc-boxShadow-lg pc-reset border-detail-themed-ofWgVp pc-borderRadius-md container-MuztBl\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-gap-8 pc-alignItems-center pc-reset textContent-ehP43r\"><a href=\"https://www.thegamebusiness.com\" data-native=\"true\" style=\"width: 48px; height: 48px;\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!IpUF!,w_96,h_96,c_fill,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep,g_auto/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fde4ef87c-a107-438a-a5b3-84b8f4920f03_1400x1400.png\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\" alt=\"The Game Business\" name=\"The Game Business\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset outline-detail-vcQLyr pub-logo-m0IFm6 static-XUAQjT\"></a><div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-pub-primary-text-NyXPlw align-center-y7ZD4w line-height-24-jnGwiv font-pub-section-headings-ukHc1v size-17-JHHggF weight-bold-DmI9lw reset-IxiVJZ\">The Game Business Show</div><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-flexDirection-column pc-reset\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-reset color-pub-secondary-text-hGQ02T align-center-y7ZD4w line-height-20-t4M0El font-text-qe4AeH size-13-hZTUKr weight-regular-mUq6Gb reset-IxiVJZ description-ij0plp\">Christopher Dring hosts interviews, in-depth analysis and special features on what's truly going on in the video games industry.</div><span hidden=\"\" data-testid=\"podcast-description\">Christopher Dring hosts interviews, in-depth analysis and special features on what's truly going on in the video